 ],
 "literal": "The sun not burning, tree shade falling, / at the foot of the mountain narrow path sand abundantly spreading, / cool rain pouring down, having abandoned us, / with the bright-edged long-speared youth, / the innocent-as-a-deer young woman went, that desert path!",
 "translation": "May the sun not burn, may the shade of trees fall, may sand be spread abundantly on the narrow path at the foot of the hills, and may cool rain pour down upon that desert path, where, leaving us behind, our young woman, innocent as a deer, has gone with the youth who holds a bright-edged, long spear!",
 "modern": "எங்களை விட்டு நீங்கி, ஒளிரும் முனையையுடைய நீண்ட வேலை ஏந்திய காளையோடு, மடப்பம் பொருந்திய மான் போன்ற இளம்பெண் சென்ற அந்தப் பாலைவன வழியில், ஞாயிறு காயாமல் மரங்களின் நிழல் படரட்டும்; மலை அடிவாரத்துச் சிறுவழியில் மணல் மிகுதியாகப் பரவட்டும்; குளிர்ந்த மழை பொழியட்டும்.",
 "explanation": "This poem is spoken by the foster-mother who is filled with grief and concern after her daughter eloped with her lover into the harsh desert path. Instead of expressing anger, her deep maternal love manifests as a series of protective wishes for the couple's journey. She prays that the fierce sun of the desert does not scorch them, that trees offer cool shade, that soft sand covers the rough mountain paths, and that refreshing rain showers down upon them. The imagery of the harsh desert path being softened by nature reflects her hope that the hardships of their new life will be eased. Key words include 'சுரன்' (desert path), 'காயாது' (without burning), and 'மடமா அரிவை' (innocent young woman).",
